export const HOW_HTML = "<div class=\"eyebrow\">isaac-perez-co · static · Vercel</div><h1 class=\"t\">How it's built</h1><div class=\"sub\">A personal homepage, six retained utility pages, no application build</div>\n<h3 class=\"sec\">The personal homepage</h3>\n<p><b>Me → Experience → My company.</b> The original portrait stays in Me. Experience includes Tinder, Nextdoor, and UC Berkeley (Electrical Engineering &amp; Computer Science). FIRSTUNIT branding appears only in My company, with one destination: <code>https://firstunit.io</code>. Personal contact closes the page quietly.</p>\n<p>The homepage does not contain an apps catalogue, photography portfolio, pricing promotion, office game, achievement UI or skills marquee. Dedicated <code>css/personal.css</code> and <code>js/personal.js</code> keep each personal-page version separate from the unchanged utility-page styles and behavior.</p>\n<h3 class=\"sec\">Filesystem</h3><pre>IsaacPerez.co/\n  index.html            Me → Experience → My company; personal contact footer\n  css/\n    personal.css        homepage only; may use site.css base tokens\n    site.css            shared utility-page styling and base tokens\n    photo.css           /photo/pricing/ only\n    design-system.css   four legal-style pages only\n    game.css            retained office chrome; not loaded by the homepage\n    rpg.css             abandoned redesign; no references\n  js/\n    personal.js         homepage theme and accessible one-time scroll reveals\n    site.js             retained utility-page motion and theme behavior\n    game.js             retained office implementation; not loaded by the homepage\n  photo/\n    (no index.html; /photo and /photo/ return 308 via vercel.json)\n    pricing/index.html  retained pricing and OfferCatalog; unpromoted on homepage\n  shootsort/index.html  retained macOS download page; unpromoted on homepage\n  roommate/\n    privacy/index.html  Quarters privacy policy\n    terms/index.html    Quarters terms\n    support/index.html  Quarters support summary and canonical-page link\n  souvenir/\n    privacy/index.html  rendered from Souvenir/docs/privacy.md\n  404.html              custom not-found page\n  images/               retained product icons\n  isaac.JPG             original portrait, used in Me and share metadata\n  Resume.pdf            old résumé, retained, unlinked and not deployed\n  favicon.svg  ndLogo.webp  tinderLogo.png\n  berkeley-seal.png     Berkeley seal, 250×250 PNG\n  sitemap.xml  robots.txt  vercel.json\n  .vercelignore         repo-only files withheld from the deployment\n  AGENTS.md             operating manual; repo-only, not served\n  .vercel/              gitignored Vercel linkage\n  docs/atlas/           data.mjs → atlas.html + SYSTEM.md; repo-only, not served</pre>\n<h3 class=\"sec\">Active and dormant code</h3>\n<p><code>js/personal.js</code> handles the homepage theme and one-time scroll reveals through IntersectionObserver and native Web Animations. Baseline content is always visible; reduced motion, unsupported APIs, focus and hash navigation skip or cancel the relevant reveals. CSS supplies a 28px portrait mask, fine-pointer hover zoom, timed underlines, arrow movements and theme transitions. Native smooth scrolling becomes immediate under reduced motion, including preference changes during the visit. No external animation dependency is added.</p><p><code>js/site.js</code> remains unchanged on retained utility pages. The inline head theme script stays before stylesheets, runtime storage access is guarded, and <code>theme</code> remains the active persistent preference.</p>\n<p><code>js/game.js</code> and <code>css/game.css</code> remain on disk without a homepage entry point or initialization. The old inline achievement integration is removed. Existing game-state keys are left alone. <code>css/rpg.css</code> and the old <code>Resume.pdf</code> remain unlinked.</p>\n<h3 class=\"sec\">Retained public pages</h3>\n<pre>/                       index.html\n/photo/pricing/         photo/pricing/index.html\n/shootsort/             shootsort/index.html\n/souvenir/privacy/      souvenir/privacy/index.html\n/roommate/privacy/      roommate/privacy/index.html\n/roommate/terms/        roommate/terms/index.html\n/roommate/support/      roommate/support/index.html</pre>\n<p>All seven remain in <code>sitemap.xml</code>. Pricing and ShootSort remain functional but are not promoted on the homepage. Legal pages and their substance remain unchanged. Existing utility-page links still resolve through native #about, #experience, #work, #firstunit and #contact targets.</p>\n<p><code>/photo</code> and <code>/photo/</code> are not pages or sitemap entries: Vercel returns HTTP 308 to <code>https://firstunit.io/fu-0001</code>. The external retired <code>capturedbyip.com</code> domain returns HTTP 301 directly to that destination (verified 2026-09-11). <code>404.html</code> handles unknown URLs and stays noindex.</p>\n<h3 class=\"sec\">Hosting and review</h3>\n<p>Vercel project <code>isaacperez</code> serves the repository root from GitHub <code>IsaacAPerez/IsaacPerez.co</code>; the project and team ids stay in the dashboard, not in this public repo. There is no application build, framework or CI. <code>vercel.json</code> retains the photo redirects and the response headers: hash-based CSP, HSTS with <code>includeSubDomains</code>, <code>nosniff</code>, <code>DENY</code> framing, referrer and permissions policy, and a same-origin CORS grant. <code>.vercelignore</code> keeps <code>AGENTS.md</code>, <code>CLAUDE.md</code>, <code>docs/</code> and <code>Resume.pdf</code> out of the deployment. A push to main publishes production; review branches and previews are not production publication.</p>\n<p>Fleet hooks enforce Conventional Commits and record activity. Preview with any static server; test header or redirect changes with a server that replays Vercel behavior. Machine-level monitoring is configured outside this repository and must not be changed as incidental website cleanup.</p>\n<h3 class=\"sec\">Rules that remain</h3>\n<p>Use exact filename case, relative homepage assets and absolute nested-page assets. Keep the original portrait and the pre-paint theme script. Do not add new external scripts, analytics, build tooling or dependencies. Do not move public URLs or alter app legal content as part of a personal-page layout change. Edit this atlas through <code>docs/atlas/data.mjs</code> and rebuild both generated views.</p>";
